---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { kayChess } from '@sparaton/content';
---
<BaseLayout title="Kay Chess | Aspheral Softworks" description="Kay Chess is an actively developed chess engine project by Aspheral Softworks.">
<section class="shell hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">Aspheral Softworks / Project</p><h1>Kay Chess</h1></div><div><span class="pill">In development</span><p class="lede">A chess engine project focused on search, evaluation, hardware-aware tuning, and careful measurement.</p><a class="button" href={kayChess.repository}>View source →</a></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">Current record</p><h2>Useful numbers, with their caveats attached.</h2></div><div class="metric-grid">{kayChess.metrics.map((metric)=><div class="metric"><span class="eyebrow">{metric.label}</span><strong>{metric.value}</strong><p class="muted">{metric.qualifier}</p><span class="pill">{metric.status}</span></div>)}</div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell grid-3"><article class="card"><h3>What Kay is</h3><p>Kay is an experimental UCI chess engine under active development. Its public repository explicitly says it has not yet reached its intended functionality or quality goals.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Auto Tune</h3><p>Auto Tune is an opt-in UCI mode that adapts thread and hash choices to available hardware while preserving manual settings for controlled testing.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>NPS is not Elo</h3><p>Nodes per second is a throughput diagnostic. Parallel search can duplicate work, so Kay does not treat a larger NPS value as equivalent to stronger chess.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="dark-band"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">Development status</p><h2>The goal is larger than the current engine.</h2></div><p class="lede muted">The project is public for development, testing, transparency, and contribution. Unfinished builds should not be represented as a completed Kay release. No download CTA is shown until an actual GitHub Release exists.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
